e the the 100 canary  rule and just put a 50/50 rule and if we  look at what our out rule looks like now  basically by using the magic of labels  and saying anything with the label of  stack prod send 50 percent of the  traffic anything with the label of stack  Canaries and 50 percent of the traffic  if we go back to that  you'll start seeing that traffic kind of  go back and forth but my ideal state so  let's say that we're happy with this the  ideal state is I want to go back to 100%  of do you know tube 2 production traffic  so again I can just delete that 50/50  rule and put that 100% production  traffic back in now I'm happy with my  deployment I'm gonna go ahead and hit  continue and I'm going to promote  version 104 to production so those last  two boxes are essentially doing a  kubernetes deployment backed by the same  service and they're deploying four pods  of that and while they're deploying we  can actually look at that application  and what it looks like today and so this  is in the middle of it deploying to  production so we can see that version  104 there's one pod deployed as canary  and then in production I'm starting to  now create another deployment for  version 104 but in the same screen I can  see it tearing down the canary and  putting a new version up until it's  ready these are gonna be red until it  waits for every single pod to be ready  before it makes them green so let's go  back to our pipeline and let's just make  sure this last one finishes that is the  central one and once the central one  finishes what we're hoping and expecting  to see is that version 104 first of all  becomes prod the new Prada and then 100%  of the traffic goes there of course that  one is the one that's taking a little  bit of time so so right now  you can see that the difference here  from the start of the demo was we had  103 as prod then we had 104 as canary  and now we have 104 as prod so just  using spinnaker and sto and kubernetes  together as is from a dev